1
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:10,193
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
Great Detective Conan
Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi

2
00:00:10,994 --> 00:00:12,396
Shin'ichi?

3
00:00:12,562 --> 00:00:13,930
Yeah.

4
00:00:14,231 --> 00:00:16,433
You can see it, too, huh?

5
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,336
There's nothing wrong with my eyes, is there?

6
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:21,238
Yeah.

7
00:00:21,438 --> 00:00:23,373
What's strange is...

8
00:00:26,843 --> 00:00:28,712
Nylon string!

9
00:00:29,046 --> 00:00:30,881
They're making fools of us.

10
00:00:31,181 --> 00:00:33,917
In an instant,
my psychic powers will awaken...

11
00:00:34,017 --> 00:00:36,219
...and, by psychokinesis,
my thoughts alone will keep it floating in air.

12
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:38,455
Geez, Dad!

13
00:00:38,588 --> 00:00:41,124
Say! Who would do such a thing and why?

14
00:00:41,224 --> 00:00:42,692
Dunno.

15
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:44,895
What I do know is...

16
00:00:44,928 --> 00:00:48,732
That the written challenge was meant for us.

17
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:49,766
"Please enjoy yourself"

18
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:52,169
There's one other thing that's clear.

19
00:00:52,636 --> 00:00:54,337
What is it you're saying I've overlooked?

20
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:58,008
That if we lose our calm in this situation
then it can be said...

21
00:00:58,141 --> 00:01:00,477
...we will surely be defeated.

22
00:01:01,511 --> 00:01:04,848
Even when you are comparatively calm,
you can't remember anything.

23
00:01:05,182 --> 00:01:06,850
Huh?!

24
00:01:07,951 --> 00:01:09,219
I know!

25
00:01:09,519 --> 00:01:10,720
My great-grandmother's birthday.

26
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:12,322
You don't know.

27
00:01:12,456 --> 00:01:15,959
This is that murder case that occurred...

28
00:01:16,093 --> 00:01:17,961
...while being broadcast live on TV.

29
00:01:18,195 --> 00:01:19,963
Ah, that one!

30
00:01:24,434 --> 00:01:25,402
"Magic"

31
00:01:25,435 --> 00:01:28,572
The person with supernatural powers,
Washimi Jiro-san!

32
00:01:36,146 --> 00:01:40,650
The psychic, Washimi Jiro-san,
rated as one of the world's best...

33
00:01:40,784 --> 00:01:44,488
...at age 7, he appeared as just a boy
on a psychic TV show.

34
00:01:44,621 --> 00:01:46,823
He made a vivid debut showing off his skills.

35
00:01:46,990 --> 00:01:52,429
Spoon bending with will-power,
spirit photography and ESP telekinesis ability!

36
00:01:52,729 --> 00:01:54,831
ESP exists.

37
00:01:55,065 --> 00:01:57,100
Tonight, let me...

38
00:01:57,601 --> 00:01:59,202
...show it to you.

39
00:01:59,269 --> 00:02:02,506
"New Sensation Battle Program
The Showdown"

40
00:02:02,639 --> 00:02:04,608
Now, let's get started tonight.

41
00:02:04,641 --> 00:02:06,309
Our New Sensation Battle Program...

42
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:07,878
- The Showdown!
- The Showdown!

43
00:02:07,911 --> 00:02:09,779
I'm your Master of Ceremonies,
Harada Takayuki, and this is...

44
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,615
His assistant, Mizutani Asako!

45
00:02:11,681 --> 00:02:14,084
- Glad you could join us!
- Glad you could join us!

46
00:02:14,451 --> 00:02:19,189
Now, today's showdown is the psychic vs.
the great detective high school student!

47
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:24,561
Will it be the self-described "born psychic,"
Washimi Jiro showing off the existence of ESP?

48
00:02:24,828 --> 00:02:28,431
Or will it be the one who boasts of
his outstanding reasoning power...

49
00:02:28,465 --> 00:02:31,735
...the great detective Kudo Shin'ichi who will
see through the secret of his ESP powers?

50
00:02:31,835 --> 00:02:36,406
My psychic ability contains
no secrets, tricks or gimmicks.

51
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:38,441
Because it isn't magic.

52
00:02:38,542 --> 00:02:40,777
But excuse me, Washimi-san.

53
00:02:40,877 --> 00:02:45,048
Truth is, I'm skeptical about ESP.
I'm sorry.

54
00:02:45,182 --> 00:02:46,917
How about you, Kudo-kun?

55
00:02:47,050 --> 00:02:49,986
If I had to say if I believed in
or didn't believe in ESP...

56
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:51,988
...well, I'd say I don't.

57
00:02:52,055 --> 00:02:54,491
I will be correcting your conceptions.

58
00:02:55,192 --> 00:02:56,960
You will tell me during this broadcast...

59
00:02:57,127 --> 00:02:59,262
"I've been mistaken"...

60
00:02:59,362 --> 00:03:01,464
...and then apologize to me.

61
00:03:02,632 --> 00:03:04,000
What's this?!

62
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:07,270
Right here we heard the psychic Washimi Jiro-san
tell the high school student great detective...

63
00:03:07,370 --> 00:03:10,607
Listen up. Unless I call "cut,"
you will never stop those cameras!

64
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:11,808
"Director - Ogasawara Isao"
- Got that?

65
00:03:11,908 --> 00:03:13,810
- Roger.
- Roger.

66
00:03:15,312 --> 00:03:16,179
Mori-san.

67
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,380
"Private Detective - Mori Kogoro"
Eh?

68
00:03:17,414 --> 00:03:20,650
You explained the gist of today's program
to Kudo-kun, didn't you?

69
00:03:20,717 --> 00:03:22,352
Don't worry, don't worry.

70
00:03:22,419 --> 00:03:25,989
More importantly, Oga-chan.
Give me more of this.

71
00:03:26,156 --> 00:03:27,924
This bouncing?

72
00:03:28,024 --> 00:03:28,825
This.

73
00:03:28,892 --> 00:03:31,228
Then, these are it. Go ahead.

74
00:03:34,731 --> 00:03:35,765
Yeah.

75
00:03:36,032 --> 00:03:38,935
These are truly ordinary spoons.

76
00:03:39,169 --> 00:03:40,704
If you would please.

77
00:03:42,539 --> 00:03:46,409
I shall bend this spoon
with my psychic abilities.

78
00:04:09,065 --> 00:04:11,835
Ah, incredible!

79
00:04:13,303 --> 00:04:17,574
It's bent. Let's compare it to one
of the ordinary spoons.

80
00:04:19,376 --> 00:04:21,144
It's different.

81
00:04:22,779 --> 00:04:24,080
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran"

82
00:04:24,147 --> 00:04:25,448
That's magnificent, isn't it?

83
00:04:25,482 --> 00:04:29,686
My psychokinesis is among
the top class levels of the world.

84
00:04:50,807 --> 00:04:52,442
- What's that!
- Incredible!

85
00:04:56,713 --> 00:05:00,917
Anyone can do that.
With skilled hands and a little practice.

86
00:05:01,151 --> 00:05:02,786
Isn't that just magic?

87
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:04,788
I bent mine with psychokinesis.

88
00:05:04,921 --> 00:05:07,190
This was an authentic spoon bending.

89
00:05:07,357 --> 00:05:08,725
Why won't you believe?

90
00:05:08,792 --> 00:05:13,897
Washimi-san, weren't you taught when you
were little that you aren't supposed to lie?

91
00:05:14,197 --> 00:05:15,732
For a long time now...

92
00:05:15,899 --> 00:05:18,368
...I've thought I couldn't forgive
a person who deceives like this.

93
00:05:18,435 --> 00:05:19,869
You should be ashamed!

94
00:05:20,937 --> 00:05:23,840
Did you... just insult me?

95
00:05:23,973 --> 00:05:27,644
Even if I did insult you, that'd be okay
since you're a fraud anyway.

96
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:29,145
I am not a fraud!

97
00:05:29,279 --> 00:05:30,780
While you guys didn't have it...

98
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:33,783
...I've had this power since I was a kid!

99
00:05:34,017 --> 00:05:35,151
Very well.

100
00:05:35,251 --> 00:05:36,986
If you're willing to go that far...

101
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:39,489
...I'll ask you to prove it here.
Right everyone?

102
00:05:39,622 --> 00:05:40,890
How about it?

103
00:05:40,924 --> 00:05:43,460
Let's see you do this, right!

104
00:05:53,370 --> 00:05:55,672
With your psychic abilities...

105
00:05:55,705 --> 00:05:57,540
...please kill me.

106
00:05:57,607 --> 00:05:59,542
Ehh!

107
00:06:00,910 --> 00:06:02,512
You won't regret it?

108
00:06:02,579 --> 00:06:03,847
Regret?!

109
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:05,949
Please let it be so.

110
00:06:06,015 --> 00:06:08,118
I'd love to see your power.

111
00:06:08,251 --> 00:06:11,454
I and everyone in the audience.

112
00:06:11,588 --> 00:06:13,156
And everyone in front of their TV sets as well!

113
00:06:13,223 --> 00:06:17,961
For treating me as a fool and taking
my psychic abilities to task as fraud...

114
00:06:18,728 --> 00:06:20,797
...you can repent for it in the afterworld.

115
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:24,000
As you wish, I will kill you!

116
00:06:24,367 --> 00:06:26,302
You other people leave.

117
00:06:47,290 --> 00:06:50,660
Oi, oi, give me a break.
What kind of program is this?

118
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:33,169
- Harada-san!
- Harada-san!

119
00:07:33,970 --> 00:07:35,638
Please hang in there, Harada-san!

120
00:07:35,672 --> 00:07:38,475
Harada-san!
Everyone, please be quiet!

121
00:07:38,942 --> 00:07:40,076
Shouldn't you stop it?

122
00:07:40,143 --> 00:07:43,179
Fool.
People don't die from ESP.

123
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:44,280
But...

124
00:07:44,481 --> 00:07:46,282
Don't worry.

125
00:07:46,349 --> 00:07:48,351
Harada-san, are you okay?

126
00:07:48,418 --> 00:07:49,452
Harada-san!

127
00:07:49,486 --> 00:07:51,454
Harada-san! Are you okay?

128
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:01,731
It can't be...

129
00:08:08,605 --> 00:08:10,073
This is bad!

130
00:08:14,644 --> 00:08:16,145
He has...

131
00:08:16,379 --> 00:08:18,481
...been killed.

132
00:08:19,215 --> 00:08:20,984
He really is dead!

133
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,566
Are you satisfied with this?

134
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:39,168
You, who made me go this far...

135
00:08:39,269 --> 00:08:41,971
...and who wouldn't believe
in ESP no matter what.

136
00:08:42,171 --> 00:08:44,274
You're all fools!

137
00:08:45,008 --> 00:08:46,309
Stupid!

138
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:50,046
I don't believe in ESP.

139
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:52,649
Are you insulting me as well?

140
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,351
This is a case of murder.

141
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:58,121
An impossible crime has happened
in front of TV cameras.

142
00:08:58,254 --> 00:09:01,624
There must certainly be some trick behind it.

143
00:09:03,359 --> 00:09:05,662
I will absolutely bring out the truth.

144
00:09:06,229 --> 00:09:08,131
There is just one truth.

145
00:09:13,369 --> 00:09:16,272
It's best not to declare
you'll reveal the truth like that.

146
00:09:16,506 --> 00:09:20,376
Because he was killed by
my psychic abilities and not some trick.

147
00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:22,378
There was definitely a trick.

148
00:09:22,545 --> 00:09:24,347
I just have to see through to what it was.

149
00:09:24,414 --> 00:09:28,518
It's not possible to see through something
that wasn't there to begin with.

150
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:34,691
If you go out in front of the cameras there
and say, "I was wrong" and apologize...

151
00:09:35,191 --> 00:09:36,893
I'll forgive you.

152
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:37,994
Live Broadcast
"The Showdown"

153
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,430
"There's just one studio door."

154
00:09:41,030 --> 00:09:42,665
"As there was no one going in or out..."

155
00:09:42,932 --> 00:09:45,868
"...this can be considered a closed-room case."

156
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:47,670
"The criminal..."

157
00:09:47,971 --> 00:09:50,573
"...is definitely in this studio!"

158
00:10:01,784 --> 00:10:04,854
Even if you investigate it,
you won't come up with anything.

159
00:10:04,988 --> 00:10:07,156
He was killed by psychic abilities.

160
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:09,158
Mine.

161
00:10:11,094 --> 00:10:14,797
Washimi-san, when I said
I would elucidate the trick...

162
00:10:14,897 --> 00:10:16,199
...I wasn't referring to your trick.

163
00:10:16,265 --> 00:10:17,433
What?

164
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,802
It's not that other side of you.

165
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:23,272
The chief suspect in Harada-san's murder...

166
00:10:23,373 --> 00:10:24,707
...is you.

167
00:10:26,476 --> 00:10:28,111
"AD - Ota Awase"

168
00:10:28,211 --> 00:10:29,679
Me?!

169
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,848
"Program Assistant
Mizutani Asako"

170
00:10:31,914 --> 00:10:33,449
It wasn't me!

171
00:10:34,417 --> 00:10:35,451
"AD - Nakamura Monjin"

172
00:10:35,485 --> 00:10:36,719
Don't joke around!

173
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,187
"Harada's Dresser
Hayashi Seiko"

174
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:40,089
Why me?

175
00:10:40,757 --> 00:10:44,160
You 5 who were on the stage then
are all suspects.

176
00:10:44,227 --> 00:10:46,129
- "Harada-san!"
- "Harada-san!"

177
00:10:47,296 --> 00:10:49,432
What do you think you're suggesting...

178
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:52,468
I thought you were
a little cleverer than that.

179
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:56,105
You ADs, Ota-san and Nakamura-san.

180
00:10:56,439 --> 00:11:00,343
Harada-san was very tyrannical
towards the both of you.

181
00:11:00,610 --> 00:11:04,814
"I told you I wanted
an unsweetened drink, you moron!"

182
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,215
"I'll kill you!"

183
00:11:06,382 --> 00:11:08,851
"You drink it. There, there..."

184
00:11:09,452 --> 00:11:13,122
There are a lot of jerks
like him in our world.

185
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:15,558
But that's not a reason to kill him!

186
00:11:15,958 --> 00:11:18,961
His assistant, Mizutani Asako-san.

187
00:11:19,328 --> 00:11:21,230
It's not ridiculous to count you
as the criminal, either.

188
00:11:21,564 --> 00:11:24,534
"Shall we have some fun tonight?"

189
00:11:25,268 --> 00:11:27,837
"Asako-chan?"

190
00:11:30,907 --> 00:11:34,177
When you've aiming for the top,
you can endure anything.

191
00:11:34,377 --> 00:11:37,747
But, if I kill someone,
that all goes poof, now doesn't it!

192
00:11:39,348 --> 00:11:41,651
His dresser, Hayashi Seiko-san.

193
00:11:41,684 --> 00:11:43,786
You, too, seem to have a motive.

194
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:48,591
"Excuse me... a friend of mine
is a fan of yours. Please sign this!"

195
00:11:48,758 --> 00:11:50,560
"Ala, I don't have a pen."

196
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,028
"I thought I had one in my purse..."

197
00:11:52,095 --> 00:11:53,129
"Pen?"

198
00:11:53,329 --> 00:11:56,032
"Ugly! Just get away from me!"

199
00:11:57,033 --> 00:11:58,801
"I'm sorry!"

200
00:12:00,303 --> 00:12:02,472
If I didn't like it,
I'd just have quit and been done with it.

201
00:12:02,538 --> 00:12:04,107
It'd be foolish to kill him.

202
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:05,942
And...

203
00:12:07,410 --> 00:12:08,911
Washimi-san...

204
00:12:22,625 --> 00:12:24,193
I withdraw my previous statement.

205
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:27,130
Washimi-san isn't a suspect.

206
00:12:27,230 --> 00:12:30,133
Yeah. Because I'm not a suspect.

207
00:12:30,199 --> 00:12:31,234
I'm the criminal.

208
00:12:31,334 --> 00:12:34,103
No. You're not even a suspect.

209
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:38,207
Because Harada-san didn't die from ESP.

210
00:12:38,908 --> 00:12:40,409
What are you saying!

211
00:12:40,610 --> 00:12:42,612
The one who killed him was me.

212
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:44,747
My psychic abilities.

213
00:12:44,914 --> 00:12:47,150
Take back what you said.

214
00:12:48,651 --> 00:12:51,988
I understand completely who
the true criminal is and what their trick was.

215
00:12:52,155 --> 00:12:54,056
No matter how many times you say it...

216
00:12:55,491 --> 00:12:57,059
It wasn't ESP.

217
00:12:58,628 --> 00:13:01,197
And you said you believed in ESP...

218
00:13:01,364 --> 00:13:02,698
What's that!?

219
00:13:02,732 --> 00:13:05,301
What I couldn't believe in then
was you, Shin'ichi!

220
00:13:05,334 --> 00:13:06,369
This is bad...

221
00:13:06,435 --> 00:13:07,503
It bent!

222
00:13:07,570 --> 00:13:09,505
- Seriously? You bent it?
- It bent, it bent!

223
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:12,608
Subtly... It bent subtly.

224
00:13:12,642 --> 00:13:13,676
Hey!

225
00:13:14,410 --> 00:13:15,812
Will you withdraw...

226
00:13:16,045 --> 00:13:18,080
...those words you said just now...

227
00:13:18,548 --> 00:13:21,551
...if I use my psychic ability
to kill your girlfriend?

228
00:13:22,685 --> 00:13:23,953
Go ahead, go ahead!

229
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:27,623
I was going to ask you
to do it once more anyway.

230
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:32,061
You'll be regretting those words
for the rest of your life.

231
00:13:32,361 --> 00:13:34,163
Hey!

232
00:13:35,998 --> 00:13:37,400
Don't worry.

233
00:13:37,767 --> 00:13:39,235
Trust me.

234
00:13:53,316 --> 00:13:54,150
Ran!

235
00:13:54,217 --> 00:13:57,053
That boy detective just went and did this!

236
00:13:58,855 --> 00:14:00,189
Hey! Leggo!

237
00:14:00,656 --> 00:14:02,291
You mustn't, Mori-san!

238
00:14:02,458 --> 00:14:03,759
Mori-san!

239
00:14:29,018 --> 00:14:30,286
Stop!

240
00:14:49,272 --> 00:14:50,406
Ran!

241
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:52,608
Sir. What are you doing here?

242
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:59,315
Jerk!

243
00:14:59,582 --> 00:15:01,584
What have you done to my daughter?

244
00:15:02,018 --> 00:15:03,786
Sir, wait. Calm down.

245
00:15:04,287 --> 00:15:05,621
Are you okay?

246
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:07,690
Ran! Ran...

247
00:15:08,791 --> 00:15:10,660
You, do something!

248
00:15:10,726 --> 00:15:14,297
Heart massage or artificial respiration
or hit her with your hand, right!

249
00:15:14,397 --> 00:15:16,332
No, you're wrong, I said.

250
00:15:16,499 --> 00:15:18,534
Enough already! I'll do it.

251
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:27,043
You pervert!

252
00:15:29,845 --> 00:15:30,780
Ran!

253
00:15:31,213 --> 00:15:32,615
What on earth is this?

254
00:15:32,648 --> 00:15:36,719
I'm sorry.
I asked her to play dead.

255
00:15:36,919 --> 00:15:38,988
What was that?!

256
00:15:39,422 --> 00:15:40,456
I'm sorry.

257
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,825
A person can't be killed by ESP.

258
00:15:42,992 --> 00:15:45,928
On what basis have you been
declaring that up till now?

259
00:15:46,062 --> 00:15:48,664
You saw me strangle Harada there, didn't you?

260
00:15:48,731 --> 00:15:53,135
My basis is the cause of death
that has appeared on Harada-san's body.

261
00:15:53,402 --> 00:15:54,837
Cause of death?

262
00:15:54,971 --> 00:15:56,038
Yes.

263
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:59,041
If Harada-san was strangled...

264
00:15:59,141 --> 00:16:01,677
...he should be showing signs of
cyanosis and extravasation of blood.

265
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:04,914
However, neither can be seen on Harada-san.

266
00:16:05,114 --> 00:16:07,917
Confirmation of that was
the sweat on his forehead.

267
00:16:08,017 --> 00:16:09,151
And then...

268
00:16:10,319 --> 00:16:13,389
Just as he was on the verge of death,
Harada-san's body jumped and he clutched his heart.

269
00:16:13,556 --> 00:16:15,224
That was a symptom of poisoning
by an intravenous injection.

270
00:16:15,291 --> 00:16:18,928
There are several types of poison
that could do that.

271
00:16:19,328 --> 00:16:23,632
Considering how quick his death was...

272
00:16:23,933 --> 00:16:27,536
...the criminal used a poison
that would cause a cardiac arrest.

273
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:30,806
For example, potassium chloride.

274
00:16:31,007 --> 00:16:35,144
Moreover, it was injected into
his jugular vein to be close to his heart.

275
00:16:35,444 --> 00:16:39,115
Harada-san's death was caused by
acute heart failure and shock.

276
00:16:39,215 --> 00:16:40,883
By the way...

277
00:16:41,017 --> 00:16:43,919
...potassium chloride is used for
death penalty executions in America...

278
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:46,722
...and its immediate effectiveness
is pre-eminent.

279
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:49,358
Harada was killed with poison?

280
00:16:49,458 --> 00:16:51,360
I don't use poisons.

281
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:54,063
Thing is, I never even got close to Harada.

282
00:16:54,230 --> 00:16:55,498
What are you saying?

283
00:16:55,564 --> 00:16:56,432
That's right.

284
00:16:56,465 --> 00:16:59,935
And that's why the suspects are
these four other than Washimi-san.

285
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:05,041
Just a moment!

286
00:17:06,409 --> 00:17:08,411
When Harada-san started his suffering...

287
00:17:08,778 --> 00:17:10,880
...there was no one touching him.

288
00:17:10,946 --> 00:17:13,249
Well, there wasn't even anyone at his side.

289
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:15,017
In a situation like that...

290
00:17:15,084 --> 00:17:17,720
...who can you say killed him with poison?

291
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:19,455
That's right.

292
00:17:19,688 --> 00:17:21,290
That's how it was.

293
00:17:21,424 --> 00:17:25,227
I guess it was my psychic powers
that killed Harada-san!

294
00:17:26,195 --> 00:17:29,298
Washimi-san, please listen to me carefully.

295
00:17:29,565 --> 00:17:32,101
That suffering Harada-san
was going through at the start...

296
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:34,103
...was just a performance.

297
00:17:34,270 --> 00:17:35,504
A performance?

298
00:17:35,771 --> 00:17:36,939
A performance?

299
00:17:37,039 --> 00:17:38,140
Yes.

300
00:17:38,941 --> 00:17:43,479
The purpose of this program was to pull
a Dokkiri on Washimi-san.
(hidden camera surprise prank)

301
00:17:43,579 --> 00:17:45,081
Isn't that right, Sir?

302
00:17:45,548 --> 00:17:48,584
Sir, you knew all about that, didn't you?

303
00:17:48,651 --> 00:17:50,586
Eh... Well, um...

304
00:17:50,719 --> 00:17:52,922
Is that right, Dad?

305
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:56,225
You made Shin'ichi appear
because you knew about that?

306
00:17:56,425 --> 00:17:58,461
Well... I didn't know all the details...

307
00:17:58,561 --> 00:18:02,698
They just mentioned,
how do I put it, a Dokkiri and...

308
00:18:02,898 --> 00:18:03,732
I'm sorry.

309
00:18:03,799 --> 00:18:05,634
Those of you with the program's staff...

310
00:18:05,835 --> 00:18:09,271
...didn't believe in Washami-san's
psychic abilities from the start.

311
00:18:09,538 --> 00:18:13,209
And so, in order to make Washami-san
a laughingstock on a live broadcast...

312
00:18:13,476 --> 00:18:15,377
...you prepared a Dokkiri for him.

313
00:18:16,712 --> 00:18:18,380
But what about the scarf?

314
00:18:18,747 --> 00:18:21,317
Didn't it look like someone was
actually strangling him with it?

315
00:18:21,417 --> 00:18:22,518
Yes.

316
00:18:22,751 --> 00:18:25,821
This scarf was evidence of the Dokkiri.

317
00:18:26,021 --> 00:18:29,825
This scarf was prepared with
a shape-memory alloy.

318
00:18:30,059 --> 00:18:32,027
Shape-memory alloys...

319
00:18:32,361 --> 00:18:35,030
...remember the shape
they were given at high temperatures.

320
00:18:35,164 --> 00:18:36,899
Even if power is added to them
and they are deformed...

321
00:18:36,966 --> 00:18:41,103
...it's possible by applying a constant temperature,
for them to return to their original shape.

322
00:18:41,570 --> 00:18:44,039
It's used for the wires in Ran's bra.

323
00:18:44,273 --> 00:18:46,642
That way, even if they are
deformed during washing...

324
00:18:47,176 --> 00:18:51,413
...once the bra is put back on, your own body
temperature will return it to its form-fitting shape.

325
00:18:51,514 --> 00:18:52,615
Excellent, aren't they?

326
00:18:52,648 --> 00:18:55,251
Idiot!
How would Shin'ichi know that?

327
00:18:55,417 --> 00:18:58,754
What? What?
Ran, you wear such a thing?

328
00:18:58,821 --> 00:19:01,257
Ah! Don't tell me you guys...

329
00:19:01,524 --> 00:19:03,259
...are in that sort of relationship!

330
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:05,828
I'm sorry.

331
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:10,332
Well, anyhow...

332
00:19:10,499 --> 00:19:12,535
...Harada-san took advantage of that property.

333
00:19:12,635 --> 00:19:14,336
While pretending to be suffering...

334
00:19:14,503 --> 00:19:17,706
...he heated the scarf with his hands,
making the ends stand up.

335
00:19:17,840 --> 00:19:22,411
That made it look as though Washami-san
was strangling him with his psychic abilities.

336
00:19:22,545 --> 00:19:23,879
Then...

337
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:26,182
What about that bruise?

338
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:30,553
This too, was evidence of the Dokkiri.

339
00:19:30,953 --> 00:19:32,121
Oh.

340
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:34,990
The bruise disappeared.

341
00:19:35,491 --> 00:19:37,893
The bruise was simply makeup.

342
00:19:38,494 --> 00:19:40,563
Ala? Then...

343
00:19:41,964 --> 00:19:44,033
He's really dead.

344
00:19:48,504 --> 00:19:49,838
I see.

345
00:19:50,005 --> 00:19:51,840
In other words, the criminal is...

346
00:19:52,575 --> 00:19:54,710
You! Makeup man!

347
00:19:56,445 --> 00:20:00,249
You're the criminal who,
under Harada-san's approval...

348
00:20:00,349 --> 00:20:03,285
...prepped this makeup, aren't you?
Eh, Makeup man?

349
00:20:03,719 --> 00:20:05,888
Such a thing!
How terrible!

350
00:20:06,021 --> 00:20:08,324
I only told him how to use that makeup.

351
00:20:08,390 --> 00:20:09,825
Oi, Sir.

352
00:20:09,892 --> 00:20:13,395
Ah... it was Harada-san who had the Makeup man
teach him about creating the bruise...

353
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:15,965
...who made it look as if he was dying and who,
when the timing was right...

354
00:20:16,065 --> 00:20:17,366
...was going to call Washimi-san a fool.

355
00:20:17,433 --> 00:20:19,969
Harada-san's the one who hatched this plan.

356
00:20:20,269 --> 00:20:22,504
Hmm... it was like that.

357
00:20:22,972 --> 00:20:25,441
But, how did this bruise
end up on her neck?

358
00:20:25,507 --> 00:20:28,777
In her case, there wasn't a chance for her
to put on this makeup, was there?

359
00:20:28,911 --> 00:20:30,579
That's right.
I guess it was you, Makeup man!

360
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:32,181
Like I said...!

361
00:20:32,848 --> 00:20:36,685
There was still some makeup
stuck to Harada-san's scarf...

362
00:20:37,019 --> 00:20:40,589
...so I asked her to
deliberately rub it into her neck.

363
00:20:40,889 --> 00:20:42,591
"Trust me."

364
00:20:45,127 --> 00:20:49,665
"Rub the scarf into your neck and act out
the same behavior Harada-san did."

365
00:20:56,538 --> 00:20:57,740
In other words...

366
00:20:57,906 --> 00:21:01,110
...while Harada-san, as part of the
composition of this Dokkiri program...

367
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,179
...was running around,
acting like he was suffering...

368
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:09,251
...someone among these 4 people
truly poisoned him.

369
00:21:10,986 --> 00:21:13,122
That's how it was.

370
00:21:13,289 --> 00:21:14,123
You're wrong.

371
00:21:14,189 --> 00:21:17,026
The criminal who killed Harada-san.

372
00:21:17,159 --> 00:21:18,527
That was...

373
00:21:18,594 --> 00:21:21,163
The criminal who killed Harada-san.

374
00:21:21,530 --> 00:21:22,898
That was...

375
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:25,868
You're wrong!

376
00:21:25,968 --> 00:21:27,102
It was me!

377
00:21:27,136 --> 00:21:29,104
It was my psychic abilities!

378
00:21:29,271 --> 00:21:30,873
Watch closely.

379
00:22:07,943 --> 00:22:09,211
Are you okay?

380
00:22:10,145 --> 00:22:13,415
Because I wasn't calm,
my aim slipped a little is all.

381
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,053
Thing is...

382
00:22:18,153 --> 00:22:20,155
...who was it among us you were
going to say gave him that poison?

383
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:21,490
Washimi-san.

384
00:22:21,890 --> 00:22:25,194
Please show me the pen in your pocket.

385
00:22:33,669 --> 00:22:37,940
The criminal used a pen-shaped syringe.

386
00:22:39,942 --> 00:22:45,047
This syringe is for my
chronic diabetes condition.

387
00:22:45,347 --> 00:22:47,483
A person wouldn't die of this.

388
00:22:50,919 --> 00:22:52,054
For pete's sake.

389
00:22:52,221 --> 00:22:54,123
The name "great detective" is crying, you.

390
00:22:54,189 --> 00:22:55,891
The one I was talking about...

391
00:22:56,725 --> 00:22:59,895
... is in that pocket.

392
00:23:07,236 --> 00:23:09,772
Why are there two of them?

393
00:23:10,472 --> 00:23:14,810
Now's your last chance
to surrender yourself to the police.

394
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:22,050
I see. Then it can't be helped.

395
00:23:24,586 --> 00:23:27,389
The true criminal who killed Harada-san...

396
00:23:27,856 --> 00:23:29,391
...is you!

397
00:23:33,362 --> 00:23:35,097
Hayashi Seiko-san!

398
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:47,443
The one who injected the poison by playing along
with Harada-san's performance was you.

399
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:50,112
I wasn't the only one at Harada-san's side.

400
00:23:50,212 --> 00:23:51,713
What's your basis for saying such a thing!

401
00:23:51,780 --> 00:23:56,452
Before going on air,
you were yelled at by Harada-san.

402
00:23:56,919 --> 00:23:58,720
"Ala, I don't have a pen."

403
00:23:58,787 --> 00:24:00,255
"I should have one in my purse..."

404
00:24:00,289 --> 00:24:01,290
"A pen?"

405
00:24:03,392 --> 00:24:06,061
"Ugly! Just get away from me!"

406
00:24:07,396 --> 00:24:08,230
"I'm sorry."

407
00:24:08,263 --> 00:24:11,600
At that time, you did have a pen.

408
00:24:12,568 --> 00:24:15,237
Even though Ran could have loaned you one...

409
00:24:15,704 --> 00:24:18,340
...you ran off to borrow a pen from someone.

410
00:24:18,407 --> 00:24:19,842
Why was that?

411
00:24:19,908 --> 00:24:21,710
I just completely forgot I had one.

412
00:24:21,743 --> 00:24:24,246
You say you completely forgot about it,
but now you have no pens.

413
00:24:24,313 --> 00:24:25,647
Why is that?

414
00:24:26,482 --> 00:24:27,983
That's...

415
00:24:28,584 --> 00:24:30,519
...because after injecting
the poison into Harada-san...

416
00:24:31,220 --> 00:24:35,190
...you snuck that pen
into Washimi-san's pocket.

417
00:24:35,524 --> 00:24:37,659
"Sir, wait. Calm down!"

418
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:39,761
"Are you okay?"

419
00:24:39,962 --> 00:24:43,398
You were intending to place
the blame on Washimi-san.

420
00:24:43,499 --> 00:24:48,270
However, you were afraid
of getting caught by me...

421
00:24:48,604 --> 00:24:51,206
...so you tried to kill
both Washimi-san and I.

422
00:25:06,555 --> 00:25:08,957
Though you continue to play the innocent...

423
00:25:09,258 --> 00:25:12,628
Well, when the investigation
checks the syringe...

424
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:15,430
...they'll find a minute amount of
your sebum DNA from it, won't they?

425
00:25:15,631 --> 00:25:18,934
For example, even if you had
wiped away your fingerprints.

426
00:25:20,102 --> 00:25:21,803
That's right.

427
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:23,839
It was me.

428
00:25:24,706 --> 00:25:26,174
Why?

429
00:25:26,441 --> 00:25:29,244
Why would you kill Harada-san?

430
00:25:29,378 --> 00:25:31,146
Why, you ask?

431
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:36,051
I believed Harada's words when
he told me I'd make my debut someday...

432
00:25:36,118 --> 00:25:38,020
...so I committed myself to Harada for 7 years.

433
00:25:38,086 --> 00:25:41,323
My body, heart and time
all went to Harada's use.

434
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:44,626
And then, finally, I was supposed to
become his assistant on this show.

435
00:25:44,726 --> 00:25:46,261
His assistant?

436
00:25:46,328 --> 00:25:47,729
That's right.

437
00:25:48,063 --> 00:25:50,432
Your position was going to be mine.

438
00:25:50,732 --> 00:25:53,035
Yet even so,
Harada went and transferred you in.

439
00:25:53,101 --> 00:25:54,469
I couldn't forgive that!

440
00:25:55,003 --> 00:25:56,805
That's why I killed him.

441
00:25:56,939 --> 00:25:59,007
- "Harada-san!"
- "Harada-san!"

442
00:26:01,977 --> 00:26:04,646
It was Harada's just desserts.

443
00:26:04,913 --> 00:26:07,783
This program was all screwed up,
so it was a nice touch.

444
00:26:08,083 --> 00:26:10,118
If I can't make my debut...

445
00:26:10,519 --> 00:26:12,354
...then I've had enough already!

446
00:26:14,389 --> 00:26:15,791
Let me go!

447
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:18,260
No one understands my feelings after all!

448
00:26:19,494 --> 00:26:24,232
I don't want to understand
a criminal's feelings.

449
00:26:25,100 --> 00:26:26,501
But...

450
00:26:26,802 --> 00:26:28,904
...there is one thing I do understand.

451
00:26:30,872 --> 00:26:33,375
For those guys who
exert themselves respectably...

452
00:26:33,909 --> 00:26:39,281
...God is certainly preparing
a reward for them.

453
00:26:40,549 --> 00:26:44,620
We don't know when that will come.

454
00:26:44,820 --> 00:26:46,622
No one knows that!

455
00:26:47,289 --> 00:26:51,593
But, that's life's Dokkiri.

456
00:26:52,361 --> 00:26:57,599
It would have been better if
you had waited just a little longer, too.

457
00:26:58,900 --> 00:27:00,702
Yes, well then, thanks for your hard work.

458
00:27:00,769 --> 00:27:02,170
Withdraw, please.

459
00:27:03,605 --> 00:27:04,673
No...

460
00:27:04,806 --> 00:27:06,241
Wait!

461
00:27:07,009 --> 00:27:08,610
You're wrong! It's not her!

462
00:27:08,677 --> 00:27:09,611
I'm a witness!

463
00:27:09,645 --> 00:27:13,448
The murderer is this psychic, Washimi Jiro!

464
00:27:13,915 --> 00:27:17,019
My psychic abilities have been restored!

465
00:27:17,252 --> 00:27:18,220
It's true...

466
00:27:18,587 --> 00:27:23,392
It's true, I've had these strange powers
ever since I was a child!

467
00:27:23,925 --> 00:27:25,394
They don't believe.

468
00:27:25,961 --> 00:27:28,497
If you don't believe,
then I'll kill all of you!

469
00:27:39,841 --> 00:27:41,109
"Magic"

470
00:27:49,584 --> 00:27:51,420
Nothing's opening!

471
00:27:51,486 --> 00:27:53,155
Eh? That's wrong?

472
00:27:53,288 --> 00:27:56,591
Fool. The real one is...

473
00:27:59,928 --> 00:28:01,930
"Dokkiri"

474
00:28:03,565 --> 00:28:05,867
"Dokkiri"

475
00:28:10,072 --> 00:28:11,740
We did it! It opened!

476
00:28:11,840 --> 00:28:13,241
Let's go.

477
00:28:23,351 --> 00:28:24,486
Again?

478
00:28:26,855 --> 00:28:28,890
Ran! Are you okay?

479
00:28:30,258 --> 00:28:32,928
Boy detective,
where did that sound come from?

480
00:28:33,061 --> 00:28:34,930
Because of the echo, I don't know.

481
00:28:46,041 --> 00:28:49,177
Sir, this time you remember, don't you?

482
00:28:52,247 --> 00:28:55,650
I will never forget the case that day;
never forget it.

483
00:29:05,594 --> 00:29:08,063
If I recall, that case was...

484
00:29:08,130 --> 00:29:09,998
"After this"
Shin'ichi's New Challenge!"

485
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:19,641
"Murder by Finger Gun!"

486
00:29:19,941 --> 00:29:22,878
"The Suspect is Kisaki Eri"

487
00:29:22,978 --> 00:29:24,880
"This Drama is Fictional"

